{"GoogleCalendarService stores the Zod safeParse result object from parseRefreshTokenResponse directly into credential.key, corrupting the DB shape and breaking subsequent credential parsing": 0.9602949023246765, "refreshOAuthTokens returns a fetch Response object on the sync path, but some integrations treat the return value as an axios response (.data) or an SDK token object (Hubspot), causing runtime type errors when syncing is enabled": 0.9574767351150513, "GoogleCalendarService reads res?.data even though the sync path of refreshOAuthTokens returns a fetch Response (no .data), causing runtime failures": 0.9267559051513672, "The sync-path comment states the sync endpoint response should only include access_token and expiry, but integrations like Zoom/Webex/Lark still require and use provider-specific fields (refresh_token, expires_in, nested data.data.*), causing failures or invalid expiry/refresh values when syncing is enabled": 0.9099315404891968, "Zoho Bigin passes credentialId into refreshOAuthTokens where the parameter is treated as a Cal.com userId for the sync endpoint payload, causing the sync service to refresh tokens for the wrong user or fail to find the user": 0.9852939248085022, "SalesforceCalendarService calls prisma.credential.update but does not import prisma in the file, causing a ReferenceError/build failure": 0.9680415987968445, "After refreshing and storing a new Salesforce access token, the code creates a jsforce.Connection using credentialKey.access_token (the pre-refresh token), causing authentication failures despite a successful refresh": 0.9594241380691528}